  {
    "sha": "3e62cea0aa576a76ec44953163beff89226a0db8",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDNlNjJjZWEwYWE1NzZhNzZlYzQ0OTUzMTYzYmVmZjg5MjI2YTBkYjg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T23:34:19Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T23:34:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(operation): read a tilted op's reference heights along its tool axis\n\nA 3+2 operation took \"Top of stock\", \"Top of model\" (and the other\nreference heights) as the setup's world Z and only subtracted the plane\norigin's Z - it never measured along the turned tool axis. A Slot at A 90\non a 10 x 30 bar put its top at 15 instead of 5 and cut air; on other\nsides of an asymmetric stock it would plunge to the wrong depth.\n\n`operation::fold_height` reads each reference height as the referenced\ngeometry's extent along the tool axis (`z_local + origin.z`, so the\nexisting `- origin.z` fold lands on the local value). It feeds the\ngeneration heights (collect_job), the Contour/Pocket/Trace section plane\n(section_z_of) and the area-controls cut plane (boundary_ctx). Fixed\nheights, untilted ops and upright tilts read exactly as before.\n\nThe viewport planes and the Heights tab echo are #2416.\n\nFixes #2389\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
      "tree": {
